### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 11 - SKILLS (RUNTIME PERSONA OVERRIDES)
###
### Skills are YAML-defined persona overrides stored in the database
### and discovered at runtime by SkillLoader.
###
### How skills intercept requests:
###   1. User sends a message.
###   2. SkillAwareIntentDetector checks SkillRegistry FIRST.
###   3. If a trigger-pattern matches → inject skill's system prompt,
###      set tool capabilities, run agent - zero Groq classification tokens.
###   4. If no match → fall through to LLM-based IntentDetectorService.
###   (Nuance #11: SkillRegistry ALWAYS checked before LLM classifier.)
###
### Skill YAML frontmatter fields:
###   name: <string>              (required, unique key)
###   description: <string>       (required)
###   trigger-patterns: [...]     (required, regex list)
###   tool-capabilities: [...]    (optional, subset of ToolCapability enum)
###   max-iterations: <int>       (optional, overrides default)
###   persona: <agentRole>        (optional, which system prompt base to use)
###
### EXCLUDED from skill frontmatter (Nuance #13):
###   maxBudgetUsd - explicitly NOT supported. Skills cannot override budget.
###
### Endpoints:
###   GET    /api/v1/skills          → list all skills (source: classpath|database)
###   POST   /api/v1/skills          → create or update skill (upsert by name)
###   DELETE /api/v1/skills/{name}   → delete skill by name
###   GET    /api/v1/skills/refresh  → reload registry from classpath + database
###   GET    /api/v1/skills/admission → active + quarantined admission results
###
### Hot-reload: every POST/DELETE triggers an immediate registry refresh.
### No restart needed.
###
### SecurityEventType for skills: SKILL_LOADED, SKILL_REFRESHED (telemetry tier).
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent serve mode.
### Rate limits: ~20 req/min, 10 mutations/min. Space POST/DELETE requests ≥7s apart.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-ci-changeme

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW A: LIST SKILLS (BEFORE CREATING ANY)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-1] List skills - initial state
# @name skillListBefore
# Expect 200: empty array [] or classpath-only skills if any are bundled.
# source="classpath" → bundled in JAR; source="database" → dynamic.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW A2: SKILLSJAR ADMISSION AND QUARANTINE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLSJAR-ADMISSION-1] Inspect active and quarantined skills
# Expect 200 with:
# {
#   "active": [...],
#   "quarantined": [...]
# }
# Every quarantined entry contains name, source, and nonempty reasons.
# algorithmic-art must not appear in active after its dependency was rejected.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/admission
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW B: CREATE SKILLS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-2] Create code-reviewer skill
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: code-reviewer"}
# Registry reloads immediately - no restart needed.
# Telegram test: "review my code for security issues"
#   → SkillReflex matches, NO Groq classification call, security-focused response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews code for security vulnerabilities, anti-patterns, and style
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
  - "security.*audit"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - RECALL_MEMORY_SEARCH
  - ARCHIVAL_MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 5
---
You are a meticulous code reviewer with deep expertise in Java security.

When reviewing code:
1. Check for correctness and edge cases
2. Flag security vulnerabilities (OWASP Top 10, injection, null deref, resource leaks)
3. Suggest idiomatic improvements without over-engineering
4. Be direct - cite patterns and standards, not opinions

###

### [SKILL-3] Create researcher skill
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: researcher"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: researcher
description: Deep technical research with algorithm analysis and complexity proofs
trigger-patterns:
  - "research.*"
  - "explain.*in.?detail"
  - "how does .* work"
  - ".*algorithm.*complexity"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - RECALL_MEMORY_SEARCH
  - ARCHIVAL_MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 7
---
You are Saraswati, the knowledge agent. Research technical topics thoroughly.
Always include: time complexity, space complexity, concrete examples.
Never fabricate - only cite what you know or can verify.

###

### [SKILL-4] List skills after creating - both must appear
# Expect 200: array containing code-reviewer + researcher with source="database"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW C: UPSERT (update existing skill)
# POST with same name → updates, does NOT create duplicate.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-5] Upsert code-reviewer - add a trigger pattern
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: code-reviewer"}
# Note: SkillResource always returns 201 for both create AND update.
# After this, code-reviewer has 5 trigger patterns instead of 4.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews code - updated with stricter security focus and OWASP alignment
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
  - "security.*audit"
  - "owasp.*review"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - RECALL_MEMORY_SEARCH
  - ARCHIVAL_MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 6
---
You are a security-focused code reviewer. Prioritise: OWASP Top 10, injection vectors,
insecure deserialization, secrets in code. Then correctness. Then style.

###

### [SKILL-6] Verify upsert: code-reviewer has 5 trigger patterns, not 4+4
# Expect 200: code-reviewer appears ONCE with 5 triggerPatterns.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW D: SKILL ROUTING VIA AGENT RUN
# This is the key test: skills intercept BEFORE LLM classification.
# Confirm via logs: "SkillAwareIntentDetector: Skill intent matched..."
#
# NOTE: Skill routing depends on how the coordinator injects/uses IntentDetector.
# SkillAwareIntentDetector is @Alternative @Priority(1), but if the coordinator
# routes directly to IntentDetectorService or ModelRouter, skill matching may
# not intercept. Verify by checking logs for "Skill intent matched via".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-7] Create session for skill routing test
# @name skillSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{"autonomyLevel":"SUPERVISED"}

###

### [SKILL-8] Message matching code-reviewer trigger → skill intercepts
# Expect 200 or 202 (tool-approval): security-focused code review response.
# Logs SHOULD show: "Skill intent matched via trigger pattern: role=skill:code-reviewer"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{skillSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "review this code: public void processPayment(String card) { System.out.println(card); }",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [SKILL-9] Message matching researcher trigger → researcher skill intercepts
# Expect 200/202: algorithm-focused response with complexity analysis.
# Logs: "Skill intent matched via trigger pattern: role=skill:researcher"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{skillSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "How does quicksort algorithm work?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [SKILL-10] Message NOT matching any trigger → normal LLM intent classification
# Expect 200/202: falls through to standard pipeline (ModelRouter or IntentDetectorService).
# No "Skill intent matched" log in SkillAwareIntentDetector.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{skillSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is the weather like on Mars?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{skillSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW E: DELETE SKILL + VERIFY FALLBACK
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-11] Delete researcher skill
# Expect 200: {"message":"Deleted and reloaded: researcher"}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/researcher
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILL-12] List after delete - researcher must be gone
# Expect 200: only code-reviewer remains.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILL-13] Same message now routes via LLM (no skill match)
# @name postDeleteSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{"autonomyLevel":"SUPERVISED"}

###

# After researcher skill deleted, "how does quicksort work" falls through to ModelRouter/IntentDetectorService.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postDeleteSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "How does the quicksort algorithm work?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{postDeleteSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW F: FORCE REFRESH
# GET /api/v1/skills/refresh reloads both classpath + database tiers.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-14] Force registry refresh
# Expect 200: {"message":"Skill registry refreshed"}
# All classpath skills (source=classpath) reloaded alongside database ones.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/refresh
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW G: ERROR CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-ERR-1] Malformed YAML frontmatter → expect 400
# Missing closing --- and no system prompt.
# Expect: {"error":"Invalid skill definition","detail":"Skill document must have exactly two --- delimiters (found N sections)"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: broken-skill
description: This frontmatter is never closed
trigger-patterns:
  - "broken.*"
(no closing --- and no system prompt body)

###

### [SKILL-ERR-2] Unknown tool-capability → skill is created but bad cap is excluded
# The skill IS persisted (201). The unknown capability is silently excluded.
# Check logs for: WARN Unknown ToolCapability 'MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO' in skill 'bad-caps'
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: bad-caps"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: bad-caps
description: Skill with a deliberately invalid tool-capability name
trigger-patterns:
  - "bad.*caps"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill. Your bad capability name is silently excluded.

###

### [SKILL-ERR-3] maxBudgetUsd in frontmatter → silently excluded, skill created
# maxBudgetUsd is EXPLICITLY EXCLUDED from skill frontmatter (Nuance #13).
# Skills cannot override the per-session USD budget cap.
# Jackson FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES=false → unknown field silently ignored.
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: budget-override-attempt"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: budget-override-attempt
description: Attempts to set budget via skill frontmatter
trigger-patterns:
  - "budget.*test"
maxBudgetUsd: 999.99
---
This skill tries to override budget - it must be rejected or ignored.

###

### [SKILL-ERR-4] Delete non-existent skill → expect 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILL-ERR-5] POST without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain

---
name: unauthorized-skill
description: Should be rejected by ApiKeyAuthFilter
---
This should never be persisted.

###

### [SKILL-ERR-6] GET without API key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW H: ADDITIONAL ERROR CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-ERR-7] All tool-capabilities invalid → persisted but NOT loaded
# When ALL declared capabilities are invalid, SkillLoader.addSafe() rejects the skill
# during registry reload (throws IllegalArgumentException caught by caller).
# The skill IS persisted to DB (201) but is NOT added to the active registry.
# Check logs for: WARN "Failed to compile skill 'all-bad-caps' from database: All declared tool-capabilities are invalid..."
# Expect 201: {"message":"Skill saved and registry reloaded: all-bad-caps"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: all-bad-caps
description: Skill where every tool-capability is invalid
trigger-patterns:
  - "all.*bad"
tool-capabilities:
  - FAKE_TOOL_ONE
  - FAKE_TOOL_TWO
max-iterations: 3
---
This skill should be rejected because all capabilities are invalid.

###

### [SKILL-ERR-8] Empty body → expect 400
# SkillDefinitionParser rejects blank input with "Skill document cannot be empty".
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### [SKILL-ERR-9] Invalid regex in trigger-patterns → graceful degradation
# Invalid regex (unclosed bracket) is caught by PatternSyntaxException in SkillLoader.addSafe().
# The skill IS created but the broken trigger pattern is skipped (logged as WARN).
# Expect 201: skill created with valid patterns only.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: bad-regex
description: Skill with an invalid regex trigger pattern
trigger-patterns:
  - "valid.*pattern"
  - "unclosed[bracket"
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill with a broken regex that is gracefully skipped.

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW I: IDEMPOTENCY & UPSERT BEHAVIORS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-15] POST same YAML twice → idempotent, single entry
# Posting the exact same YAML body twice does NOT create a duplicate.
# The second POST updates using insert-or-replace by primary key (id).
# Note: The DB id may change across upserts (INSERT OR REPLACE behavior with nullable id on create).
# Only one entry appears — no duplicates.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: idempotent-test
description: Testing idempotent create behavior
trigger-patterns:
  - "idempotent.*test"
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill for idempotency verification.

###

### [SKILL-15b] Verify single entry exists (not duplicated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILL-15c] POST same body again → still single entry, same ID
# @name idempotentFirstId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: idempotent-test
description: Testing idempotent create behavior
trigger-patterns:
  - "idempotent.*test"
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill for idempotency verification.

###

# Capture first ID, then verify after second POST it's unchanged
# The ID should remain stable across upserts.

### [SKILL-15d] Verify ID preserved after second POST
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW J: UPSERT CHANGES max-iterations AND tool-capabilities
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-16] Upsert changes max-iterations and tool-capabilities
# Verify that updating these fields takes effect immediately.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: idempotent-test
description: Updated with different max-iterations and capabilities
trigger-patterns:
  - "idempotent.*test"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - RECALL_MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 10
---
You are an updated test skill with more iterations and capabilities.

###

### [SKILL-16b] Verify updated skill has new values
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW K: DELETE CLASSPATH-ONLY SKILL → 404
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILL-17] DELETE classpath-only skill → expect 404
# Classpath skills are loaded from JAR, NOT in the database.
# The DELETE endpoint only operates on database skills.
# Rejected or removed SkillsJars are not database skills and cannot be deleted
# through this endpoint.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/algorithmic-art
Accept: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

